{
  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_031 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieved 0.532 acc / 0.517 F1, while config_024 (rna_only, scvi_n200, singleprofile) achieved 0.520 acc / 0.498 F1. The multimodal gain over RNA-only is small (+0.012 acc), and we have only tested one RNA encoder (scvi_n200). Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether the RNA encoder choice (scvi_n200 vs. scgpt) materially affects performance, which is a fundamental representation decision that will influence all future multimodal experiments. Question tested: config_037 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, concat) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_031, isolating the effect of RNA encoder while holding image encoder, profile setting, and fusion constant. Why best next experiment: Under a limited budget, understanding whether RNA representation quality is a key lever (vs. fusion strategy or profile setting) is the highest-information question. If scgpt significantly outperforms or underperforms scvi_n200, it reshapes the search direction for all subsequent multimodal experiments. If they are similar, we can deprioritize RNA encoder and focus on fusion or multiprofile next."
}

